# Linear Representation Analysis

Status: concluded on 2026-09-07.

## Objective

Compare class geometry before and after the trained `768 -> 3` linear classifier on fold 0's untouched outer-test pairs.

## Hypothesis

The signed pair representation

```text
resume_embedding - jd_embedding
```

may already organize resume-JD pairs by fit label. A learned linear projection from 768 dimensions to the three class logits may preserve or improve that class organization without intermediate hidden layers.

## Reproduce

```bash { name=train-linear-fold-zero }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/train_classifier.py \
  --device cuda \
  --fold 0 \
  --max-epochs 50 \
  --patience 50 \
  --experiment resume-jd-linear
```

```bash { name=analyze-representations }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/evaluate_classifier.py --fold 0
```

## Run

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Parent MLflow run | `6297deae60fd4001b6925428e47d0370` |
| Fold MLflow run | `687cbb87d86a47b7ab50e548cbf1b256` |
| Outer-test rows | 10,644 |
| Before representation | Standardized resume embedding minus JD embedding |
| After representation | Three classifier logits |
| t-SNE perplexity | 30 |
| t-SNE seed | 42 |

## Representation Metrics

| Metric | Before | After |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| 10-neighbor label purity | 0.7604 | 0.6122 |
| Silhouette score | -0.0491 | -0.0476 |
| Intra-class cosine similarity | 0.0142 | 0.0398 |
| Inter-class cosine similarity | 0.0097 | -0.0364 |
| Cosine separation | 0.0045 | 0.0762 |
| t-SNE trustworthiness | 0.9978 | 0.9995 |

## Held-Out Classification

| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 | Support |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| No Fit | 0.8422 | 0.5112 | 0.6362 | 7,802 |
| Potential Fit | 0.2476 | 0.3203 | 0.2793 | 2,079 |
| Good Fit | 0.1364 | 0.5754 | 0.2205 | 763 |

Overall outer-test accuracy is `0.4785`; macro F1 is `0.3787`.

## Plot

```text
data/analysis/6297deae60fd4001b6925428e47d0370/fold_0/tsne_before_after.png
```

Both t-SNE panels show substantial mixing between true classes. The linear projection increases sampled cosine separation but lowers local 10-neighbor label purity. The plot and JSON report are logged under the fold MLflow run's `representation` artifacts.

## Interpretation

- The pre-training t-SNE contains more compact geometric islands than the logit t-SNE.
- True-label colors remain mixed within those islands, so the visible pre-training structure is not clean three-class separation.
- Local 10-neighbor label purity falls from `0.7604` to `0.6122` after the linear projection.
- Both true-label silhouette scores are negative, before and after training.
- The linear classifier reaches `0.4785` outer-test accuracy and `0.3787` macro F1 on fold 0.
- The two t-SNE layouts were fitted independently. Their absolute positions, distances, and island shapes are not directly comparable; the numerical neighborhood and classification metrics provide the comparison.

## Decision

Do not use the signed difference alone with a `768 -> 3` linear projection as the final resume-JD scoring model. In this experiment, the projection discards useful local structure without producing clean true-label clusters or adequate held-out classification.

This result does not reject the frozen EmbeddingGemma document embeddings themselves. It rejects the tested pair-comparison function and classifier configuration:

```text
(resume_embedding - jd_embedding) -> linear classifier
```

The next pair-comparison technique remains undecided and must be discussed before another implementation or experiment is run.
